he money they get. No body will Invest in India, when capital costs itself (such as land) are too expensive. Industries create lots of employment. A Tata plant employing 10,000 people in its plant provides indirect employment for another 1,00,000. You want to see examples. Detroit? A whole city is dependent on Automobile plants!!!! Reporters, newspapers please be responsible.'),(10229,'dogtimemedia.com','guest8594','2008-10-05 22:30:21','crying as I wright this. my dog keeps peeing in my bed right where I sleep. what does it mean'),(10230,'dogtimemedia.com','guest8594','2008-10-05 22:30:42','write'),(10231,'www.hulu.com','guest8763','2008-10-05 22:53:12','HI'),(10232,'www.hulu.com','guest8763','2008-10-05 22:53:22','COOL'),(10233,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=25c3d8e9-74e5-43e8-94d3-dd1d2be21992&&Headline=Whose+brakes+failed?','guest9690','2008-10-06 03:18:18','Its a good counter artical.e Till now Tata\\\'s have been made the sufferer and Trinamool the tormentor. but this article puts the points in perspective. I guess Tata is also like any other businessman. Noone has time to think about poor.'),(10234,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=25c3d8e9-74e5-43e8-94d3-dd1d2be21992&&Headline=Whose+brakes+failed?','guest8370','2008-10-06 04:58:31','If buying land was so easy then West Bengal government could have compensated land for land but that is not possible and someone in Detroit may not realise the ground realities in Bengal--all in all it is better that Buddha got out of this mess as the future would have brought more misery and this would have haunted him to his death'),(10235,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=25c3d8e9-74e5-43e8-94d3-dd1d2be21992&&Headline=Whose+brakes+failed?','guest2961','2008-10-06 05:27:01','But what he has proved, beyond a shadow of doubt, is that he is no Jamshed Tata.\r\n-------- >'),(10236,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=25c3d8e9-74e5-43e8-94d3-dd1d2be21992&&Headline=Whose+brakes+failed?','guest2961','2008-10-06 05:28:06','Is todays politicians Pt. Nehru.. time has changed and so the priorities ... now we have mamta and even people perception has changed'),(10237,'dogtimemedia.com','guest9671','2008-10-06 07:32:48','I need a name for a female pit. She is blonde with hazel eyes. I want her first name to be Sydney.'),(10238,'dogtimemedia.com','guest9671','2008-10-06 07:36:33','I had a dog that wet my bed when I would go to work.  She wanted more attention.'),(10239,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=&id=b2ac5f65-8849-436f-a3d5-6cf8ceba5b02&&Headline=WhoÃ¢â‚¬â„¢s+got+talent?','guest6110','2008-10-06 07:44:16','jkj'),(10240,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=&id=b2ac5f65-8849-436f-a3d5-6cf8ceba5b02&&Headline=WhoÃ¢â‚¬â„¢s+got+talent?','guest6110','2008-10-06 07:44:18','lkl'),(10241,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=&id=d2b6c026-913c-432a-aa28-c7289c8ab2c7&&Headline=Univ+students+may+get+to+rate+teachers','guest7815','2008-10-06 07:51:45','University of Mysore already has done this exercise twice in the last 4 years. Why does the press try to sensationalise such common activities?'),(10242,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=25c3d8e9-74e5-43e8-94d3-dd1d2be21992&&Headline=Whose+brakes+failed?','guest5950','2008-10-06 08:11:51','This article makes little sense to me.\nit describes everything to be the industries job. if tata should have set up a coop then wat do we need the state government and mamta banerjee for? tata should have just gone to singur n sold shares in exchange for land?\nwasnt it the job of the state goverment to take more rent and distribute it to the farmers? wasnt it mamta banerjees job to do more constructive things than throw farmers on the streets to be beaten by the police? we dont elect leaders to go on strike n make morchas, we elect them to lead, and they should have lead all including tata who is also a citizen n not a leader.why shud tata propose plans/deals to mamta? her only job is to be counterproductive?\nI am not even sure the author really understands the dynamics of setting up that big a plant. 90% complete doesnt mean just the shed, severel hundred man hours would have been invested in planning, making the business model, figuring and laying the logistics, those count as losses too. n ot to mention re'),(10243,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=25c3d8e9-74e5-43e8-94d3-dd1d2be21992&&Headline=Whose+brakes+failed?','guest5950','2008-10-06 08:15:46','location of the engineers and workers that might have already been present to supervise and test the installations.'),(10244,'dogtimemedia.com','Dr. Tubbs','2008-10-06 08:47:50','how do i know when my dog is ready to walk with me off leash?'),(10245,'dogtimemedia.com','guest5417','2008-10-06 09:00:21','when he responds to you regularly when you call him'),(10246,'dogtimemedia.com','guest5687','2008-10-06 09:08:01','ello'),(10247,'dogtimemedia.com','Dr. Tubbs','2008-10-06 09:08:51','i\\\'m just a little worried that out in the park, he\\\'ll get distracted -- even if i have really good treats with me'),(10248,'dogtimemedia.com','guest5687','2008-10-06 09:08:57','I thought you were always suppose to have a dog on a leash??'),(10249,'dogtimemedia.com','Dr. Tubbs','2008-10-06 09:09:09','some parks are off leash'),(10250,'dogtimemedia.com','guest5687','2008-10-06 09:09:41','Just take him to a fenced in dog park'),(10251,'dogtimemedia.com','guest6076','2008-10-06 10:02:07','My dog is throwing up alot for some reason'),(10252,'dogtimemedia.com','guest6076','2008-10-06 10:02:25','Im getting nervous'),(10253,'dogtimemedia.com','guest6076','2008-10-06 10:03:03','Also I have to do this thing on bloodhounds'),(10254,'dogtimemedia.com','guest6076','2008-10-06 10:03:17','Anybody on?'),(10255,'www.