?sectionName=HomePage&id=568ef100-067b-4811-800c-0e59efcfd714&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=Polls+apart','guest2087','2008-10-11 08:00:39','Are the Indian electorate and the American one really that poles apart? For one, the issues thrashed about themselves are so different, responses to them are necessarily different-India remains saddled with \\\'basic\\\' problems of roti, kapda, makan, basic infrastructure, health and education-issues that cannot really have very varied ideological underpinnings. America, having met these basic goals, now face issues such as  the energy crisis, ecology, credit and investment, immigration policies, and values such as abortion rights, gay rights, women power-issues that are necessarily approached variably. Two, consider the electorate-in India where a minority can afford to split hair over the finer calibrations of the caste and quota issue-I mean what percentage of Indians have access to newspapers and a television or the leisure time to analyse those issues? And finally, even in the U.S., the lament is that the masses (as opposed to the elite media analysts, academics, intellectuals) are swayed more by appeals to'),(10650,'dogtimemedia.com','guest9192','2008-10-11 08:03:10','hi'),(10651,'dogtimemedia.com','guest9192','2008-10-11 08:03:39','hi'),(10652,'dogtimemedia.com','guest9192','2008-10-11 08:03:57','anybody on?'),(10653,'dogtimemedia.com','guest9192','2008-10-11 08:04:53','guess not'),(10654,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=568ef100-067b-4811-800c-0e59efcfd714&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=Polls+apart','guest2087','2008-10-11 08:07:55','Are the Indian electorate and the American one really that poles apart? For one, the issues thrashed about themselves are so different, responses to them are necessarily different-India remains saddled with \\\\\\\'basic\\\\\\\' problems of roti, kapda, makan, basic infrastructure, health and education-issues that cannot really have very varied ideological underpinnings. America, having met these basic goals, now face issues such as the energy crisis, ecology, credit and investment, immigration policies, and values such as abortion rights, gay rights, women power-issues that are necessarily approached variably. Two, consider the electorate-in India where a minority can afford to split hair over the finer calibrations of the caste and quota issue-I mean what percentage of Indians have access to newspapers and a television or the leisure time to analyse those issues? Third, even in the U.S., the lament is that the masses (as opposed to the elite media analysts, academics, intellectuals) are swayed more by appeals to th'),(10655,'dogtimemedia.com','guest9192','2008-10-11 08:29:59','cp,e on talk'),(10656,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?id=075edbff-0005-40f9-a45b-a308d00bf8e3&ParentID=b4695384-7291-4305-a877-cc721f3f8838&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=Factbox:+Christians+in+India,+a+tiny+group','guest5000','2008-10-11 09:21:18','\\\"* Christians make up 2.3 percent of India\\\'s billion-plus population, which is predominantly Hindu.\\\" - This is a very western (ignorant) way of looking India as a whole.'),(10657,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?id=075edbff-0005-40f9-a45b-a308d00bf8e3&ParentID=b4695384-7291-4305-a877-cc721f3f8838&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=Factbox:+Christians+in+India,+a+tiny+group','guest5000','2008-10-11 09:22:22','Also it is not the revival of Hindu nationalism that has caused intolerance on Christians rather it is a regional fundamentalism.'),(10658,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3093','2008-10-11 10:29:33','Which dog do you think is best as a \nguard dog?'),(10659,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3093','2008-10-11 10:30:20','Is any body lo\nged on'),(10660,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/FullcoverageStoryPage.aspx?id=0fdb1dc9-a06c-491e-b90a-7169d096f85bTerrorStrikesDelhi_Special&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=My+hometown+is+changing','guest9685','2008-10-11 11:20:22','GREATLY SAID KHUSHWANT SINGH, WE NEED JOURNALIST LIKE YOU WHO WOULD SPEAK FOR THE DOWNTRODDEN, THE OPPRESSED AND THOSE INNOCENT PEOPLE BEING FRAMED IN THE NAME OF RELIGION.  THANK YOU'),(10661,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=38bd540e-98aa-4041-aaf6-88717cb2b6c1&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=A+time+for+Father+Terry','guest1128','2008-10-11 12:56:52','To answer of question in the end, I would just say that voices of peace are always quieter. By the very nature they are raised in response to some violent act. They are labeled seculars as long as they criticize their own faith of hardliners if they criticize someone else\\\' faith. They fade away because peace-lovers either leave the march themself in frustration or no one listens because unlike violent protesters they do not generate juicy news.'),(10662,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=38bd540e-98aa-4041-aaf6-88717cb2b6c1&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=A+time+for+Father+Terry','guest4583','2008-10-11 13:56:37','Here in U.S., this'),(10663,'dogtimemedia.com','guest8786','2008-10-11 14:20:04','hello'),(10664,'dogtimemedia.com','guest8786','2008-10-11 14:20:10','Anyone in here?'),(10665,'dogtimemedia.com','guest8786','2008-10-11 14:20:16','Just me?'),(10666,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3327','2008-10-11 14:31:57','hello'),(10667,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3327','2008-10-11 14:32:34','anybody here'),(10668,'dogtimemedia.com','guest6202','2008-10-11 14:42:52','how old is the best for puppy to leave their mums'),(10669,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=f5d6cfa8-fc71-40d0-a76a-64f41454c9e9&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=Missionary+position','guest3413','2008-10-11 14:44:10','this article is good.'),(10670,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=f5d6cfa8-fc71-40d0-a76a-64f41454c9e9&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=Missionary+position','guest3413','2008-10-11 14:44:35','interesting....'),(10671,'bharat-voice.com','guest3413','2008-10-11 14:45:19','Have you seen it....?!?!?!?!'),(10672,'dogtimemedia.com','guest4443','2008-10-11 16:39:59','hi'),(10673,'dogtimemedia.com','guest4443','2008-10-11 16:41:27','how much time do a dog need to spend time to come out pregnant while there in heat?'),(10674,'dogtimemedia.com','guest4443','2008-10-11 16:43:30','any one here?'),(10675,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=f5d6cfa8-fc71-40d0-a76a-64f41454c9e9&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=Missionary+position','guest3335','2008-10-11 17:06:32','nope i dont think so'),(10676,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=f5d6cfa8-fc71-40d0-a76a-64f41454c9e9&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=Missionary+position','guest3335','2008-10-11 17:07:13','I HATE THIS SENTENSE - Itâ€™s harder still to argue that Hinduism, which survived centuries of Buddhist influence, Muslim rule and the British empire, faces any significant threat from the activities of missionaries in Orissa, Madhya Pradesh or Karnataka.'),(10677,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=f5d6cfa8-fc71-40d0-a76a-64f41454c9e9&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=Missionary+position','guest3335','2008-10-11 17:07:59','absolutely it is a matter of concern. the religion survived during muslims/british was because there was a  fight to sustain the religion..'),(10678,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=f5d6cfa8-fc71-40d0-a76a-64f41454c9e9&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=Missionary+position','guest3335','2008-10-11 17:09:10','it was becaus of the great saints who helped it to survive.. and now we need the bajrang to sustain the religion.'),(10679,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/FullcoverageStoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=df243d5a-bf69-4806-8d93-364c16db33c1AustraliatourofIndia_Special&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&IsCricket=true&Headline=Twist+in+tail','guest3317','2008-10-11 17:22:14','I believe Dhoni is not giving 100% in tests for reasons best known to him. An example is the Sydney test, which I watched and think he was looking to throw away his wicket.'),(10680,'www.lauriescullymusic.co.uk/contactzone.html','lauriescully','2008-10-11 17:38:43','Welcome to the LSM ContactZone!'),(10681,'www.lauriescullymusic.co.uk/contactzone.html','teddytester','2008-10-11 17:40:52','iz doin me bit!'),(10682,'www.lauriescullymusic.co.uk/contactzone.html','lauriescully','2008-10-11 17:42:13','Well done Ted Ur Pure Class!'),(10683,'www.lauriescullymusic.co.uk/contactzone.html','teddytester','2008-10-11 17:43:08','summut like that!'),(10684,'www.lauriescullymusic.co.uk/contactzone.html','teddytester','2008-10-11 17:44:44','ok it works - next!'),(10685,'www.lauriescullymusic.co.uk/contactzone.html','lauriescully','2008-10-11 17:46:13','That\\\'s 4 Another Time.... CU Later....TTFN!'),(10686,'www.lauriescullymusic.co.uk/contactzone.html','teddytester','2008-10-11 17:46:45','BFN!'),(10687,'www.lauriescullymusic.co.uk/contactzone.html','lauriescully','2008-10-11 17:46:58','.......................'),(10688,'www.lauriescullymusic.co.uk/contactzone.html','lauriescully','2008-10-11 17:47:04','....'),(10689,'www.lauriescullymusic.co.uk/contactzone.html','lauriescully','2008-10-11 17:47:07','...'),(10690,'www.lauriescullymusic.co.uk/contactzone.html','lauriescully','2008-10-11 17:47:08','..'),(10691,'www.lauriescullymusic.co.uk/contactzone.html','lauriescully','2008-10-11 17:47:09','.'),(10692,'www.johnwarden.lauriescullymusic.co.uk/jwxxspxxareaxxflx/jwsxxsecret.html','lauriescully','2008-10-11 18:05:32','Hi There John.... Yep it\\\'s Yet Another Chat Application!'),(10693,'www.lauriescullymusic.co.uk/info.html','lauriescully','2008-10-11 18:14:44','Welcome To LSM - Info!'),(10694,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?id=329c6411-5fe3-4150-9ed6-db4a9b5a3bec','guest6888','2008-10-11 18:33:49','Great article, but needs some factual modifications. Parsis derive their ethnic name from their nation Parsa (called Persia in the west). The conquering arabs could not pronounce \\\"P\\\"; so the \\\"P\\\" was replaced by \\\"F\\\", the language name becoming \\\"farsi\\\".'),(10695,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?id=329c6411-5fe3-4150-9ed6-db4a9b5a3bec','guest6888','2008-10-11 18:37:51','Importantly Parsis escaped to India a few centuries after the arab invasion, when it became very clear that the new converts from their own countrymen were pledged to hound them to oblivion. This estimation was historically validated when only 5000 Parsis were counted in the census of 1850.'),(10696,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?id=329c6411-5fe3-4150-9ed6-db4a9b5a3bec','guest6888','2008-10-11 18:41:48','The Parsis of today (in India) are remnants of many individual migrations from different parts of the Persian empire to places in Gujrat (like the original migration) & to Sind & Punjab. Surnames such as Dhalla & Gagrat attest to this fact, as well as the oral tradition of Kisse e Sanjan which is a mish-mash of the stories of separate groups.'),(10697,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=f5d6cfa8-fc71-40d0-a76a-64f41454c9e9&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=Missionary+position','guest2790','2008-10-11 18:56:06','Mr. Sanghvi,'),(10698,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=f5d6cfa8-fc71-40d0-a76a-64f41454c9e9&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=Missionary+position','guest2790','2008-10-11 18:56:18','What you said is like fantasy'),(10699,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=f5d6cfa8-fc71-40d0-a76a-64f41454c9e9&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=Missionary+position','guest2790','2008-10-11 18:58:41','Come to the reality. Do you think that it is ethical to convert people by some means inspite knowing the fact that, by doing so you are dividing the family members, dividing the villagers, dividing a community etc.'),(10700,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=f5d6cfa8-fc71-40d0-a76a-64f41454c9e9&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=Missionary+position','guest1693','2008-10-11 19:03:11','this is one of the very few decent articles by vir'),(10701,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=f5d6cfa8-fc71-40d0-a76a-64f41454c9e9&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=Missionary+position','guest1693','2008-10-11 19:05:22','While I agree that Hindus should not be attacking Christians (if that is true and not instigated by them attacking us first), I don\\\'t think he is right in that Hinduism does not face any significant threat from the activities of missionaries in Orissa, Madhya Pradesh or Karnataka.'),(10702,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=f5d6cfa8-fc71-40d0-a76a-64f41454c9e9&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=Missionary+position','guest1693','2008-10-11 19:06:49','It definitely does. Hinduism survived centuries of Buddhist influence because Buddhist teachings themselves rooted in Hinduism. Muslim and British rule on the other hand greatly hampered and restricted Hindu beliefs.');
INSERT INTO `chat` VALUES (10703,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=f5d6cfa8-fc71-40d0-a76a-64f41454c9e9&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=Missionary+position','guest2790','2008-10-11 19:07:46','You may be a city grown English educated individual for whome, whatever exist in the western society is beutiful and great and whatever exist in Hindusim is crazy and communal. Let me tell you I am from Orissa and now staying in USA. Believe me, people of my state are more secular and ethical. In the western world everybody looks the world from the christianism window. You should appreciate the fact that we as Hindus worship everything who has done benifit to the society. Go and meet my mother, you will find that she prays Jesus, Boodha along with lord Rama and Krishna.  I have the first hand experience of the fact that the missonary people create hatreds\\\' among the hindus. One of my friend along with his brothers have converted to christianism. As a matter if fact, his parent who are still hindus, don\\\'t take food in their own son\\\'s house may be because of agony and frustration. Do you want this kind of division among the people. Grow up you so called secular English journalists.'),(10704,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=f5d6cfa8-fc71-40d0-a76a-64f41454c9e9&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=Missionary+position','guest1693','2008-10-11 19:10:45','Islamic rulers burnt Hindu literature, etc. the list is endless. British and other Christians to this day propogate Macaulayism. Our Hindu truths are called Hindu mythology and their stories are called Biblical facts. If that is not harming our religion, what is?'),(10705,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=f5d6cfa8-fc71-40d0-a76a-64f41454c9e9&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=Missionary+position','guest1693','2008-10-11 19:13:06','Hindus believe in true freedom - you can be a athiest, agnostic, idol worshipper, Arya Samaji, etc. and still be Hindu. Islam and Christianity are a lot more restrictive. It is like comparing democracy to a dictatorship and the dictator telling you why democracy wouldn\\\'t work for you.'),(10706,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=f5d6cfa8-fc71-40d0-a76a-64f41454c9e9&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=Missionary+position','guest1693','2008-10-11 19:17:32','Every person who believes in freedom of thought and religion could be called a Hindu. Well, we\r\n are so open-minded that even though we are not Hindu (we are Hindi and Sanatan Dharmi or Arya Samaji, etc.), we accepted being called that and most people don\\\'t even understand that.'),(10707,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=38bd540e-98aa-4041-aaf6-88717cb2b6c1&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=A+time+for+Father+Terry','guest1693','2008-10-11 19:28:41','Good article. The Father Terry of your article was open to other religions (atleast Hinduism to some extent), but the cause for these attacks are people who are intolerant. Christian missionaries converting Hindus are intolerant and fascist. I don\\\'t even know what to call those Hindus attacking Christians. I mean I support nationalism, but come on - why on earth are you hurting somebody or attacking their places of worships. We are better than Muslims and Christians.'),(10708,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=f5d6cfa8-fc71-40d0-a76a-64f41454c9e9&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=Missionary+position','guest1488','2008-10-11 19:34:34','Dear Salvi,'),(10709,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=f5d6cfa8-fc71-40d0-a76a-64f41454c9e9&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=Missionary+position','guest1488','2008-10-11 19:39:08','Dear Salvi, I agree with you we should be ashamed about attacks on Christians; They write so much filthy about Hinduism and distribute pamplets nook and corner of INDIA that doesn\\\'t matter? If they wish to learn exactly about HINDUISM let them come forward, have dialogue with our religious leaders, then they will come to know exactly about us!! I appreciate the Christians PR work in maligning HINDUS all around the globe! Mr. Salvi, give the clear picture on both sides and talk. I reiterate we have no right to attack anybody! When did HINDUS attack out siders! We are so called Secularist and believe in piece hence we are prosperous all around the globe'),(10710,'dogtimemedia.com','guest9934','2008-10-11 19:53:27','hello'),(10711,'dogtimemedia.com','guest9934','2008-10-11 19:54:17','anyone else just give their shiba a bath?'),(10712,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=f5d6cfa8-fc71-40d0-a76a-64f41454c9e9&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=Missionary+position','guest3671','2008-10-11 21:25:05','Hello....forget history...forget past...if you follow that better to stay in jungle n caves humanities made lots of progress and the fact is forcible conversion is illegal period.'),(10713,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=f5d6cfa8-fc71-40d0-a76a-64f41454c9e9&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType1=1&SeriesID1=1212&PrimaryID=4813&Headline=Missionary+position','guest3671','2008-10-11 21:25:47','You serve poor no harm that.....but why to convert..?'),(10714,'dogtimemedia.com','guest5643','2008-10-11 22:23:13','hello'),(10715,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=&id=ca8d873b-da49-41c0-94db-265567068274&MatchID1=4813&TeamID1=6&TeamID2=1&MatchType