4','2008-10-28 12:13:23','you can have the dew claw removed'),(14993,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-10-28 12:13:57','i\\\'m sure the dog is still wonderful!'),(14994,'dogtimemedia.com','todddog1','2008-10-28 12:14:43','naw.. i\\\'m gonna keep the dog and his funny dew claw just the way they are.'),(14995,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-10-28 12:15:08','he\\\'ll be unique!'),(14996,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3488','2008-10-28 12:16:42','hes 9 wks andd i must say he is good with my kids and they love him so he is for keeps but my vet tried to tell me to get rid of him because akitas are ment to be aggressive'),(14997,'dogtimemedia.com','todddog1','2008-10-28 12:17:04','does the akita shed much?'),(14998,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3488','2008-10-28 12:18:15','only 2 times a year and if you brush them every day you dont see any hair on your floor'),(14999,'dogtimemedia.com','todddog1','2008-10-28 12:19:30','not bad at all.'),(15000,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-10-28 12:19:39','i agree not bad at all'),(15001,'dogtimemedia.com','todddog1','2008-10-28 12:21:13','what\\\'s the puppy\\\'s name?'),(15002,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3488','2008-10-28 12:21:18','one good thing about the breed they dont bark unless they get scared i have only heard bailey bark once in 2 wks'),(15003,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-10-28 12:22:09','yes i have read that akitas don\\\'t bark much, but when they do pay attention'),(15004,'dogtimemedia.com','DogTimeMediaMVN2','2008-10-28 12:24:19','hi'),(15005,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3488','2008-10-28 12:24:28','i think akitas are given a bad name if you treat them right they wont be aggressive'),(15006,'dogtimemedia.com','todddog1','2008-10-28 12:46:07','just like pit bulls'),(15007,'dogtimemedia.com','guest9568','2008-10-28 12:46:30','Got a very jumpy & hyper retriever 8 months old any suggestions to make him stop??'),(15008,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-10-28 12:47:08','has he been neutered?'),(15009,'dogtimemedia.com','guest9568','2008-10-28 12:47:28','No.  I am going to show him.'),(15010,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-10-28 12:48:14','maybe obedience school would help to train him'),(15011,'dogtimemedia.com','guest2777','2008-10-28 12:50:40','one thing i do to make a dog stop jumping is make it hard for them to do by raising up one knee pre-emptively and say \\\"No.\\\"'),(15012,'dogtimemedia.com','guest9568','2008-10-28 12:50:48','Thanks... i have tried DogStar which was a waist of time. Pinch collar, then the Ceaser millian Illusion Collar now.  All seem to be non-detourants & he is constantly pulling on the leash. I am trying another trainer Nov. 7th so hopefully he can give me tips. But, for now I am at a loss & the jumping & trying to nip hands is driving me crazy. He is good for a bit then flips out. I have a 12 year old golden at home & he never acting like an animal out of a cage ever.'),(15013,'dogtimemedia.com','guest2777','2008-10-28 12:50:48','eventually it sinks in lol'),(15014,'dogtimemedia.com','guest9568','2008-10-28 12:51:39','The knee thing I tried he keeps jumping he just goes to the opposite leg your not lifting to block him.'),(15015,'dogtimemedia.com','guest2777','2008-10-28 12:52:39','just gotta be consistant with it (and quick sometimes) if he sits on command that\\\'s a good time for it'),(15016,'dogtimemedia.com','guest2777','2008-10-28 12:53:11','if you spend a lot of time away from the dog (at work, school etc.) one good tip is to sit with the dog for about 10 minutes before an absence'),(15017,'dogtimemedia.com','guest2777','2008-10-28 12:53:23','but pay no attention to it at all'),(15018,'dogtimemedia.com','guest2777','2008-10-28 12:53:29','do the same when you get home'),(15019,'dogtimemedia.com','guest2777','2008-10-28 12:53:46','if you do that for a while the dog will be much calmer about absences and not get so hyper'),(15020,'dogtimemedia.com','guest9568','2008-10-28 12:53:49','Cool... that sounds great I will try it again then. Thanks for all the advice everyone I do love him so & have no intentions on getting rid of him . Overall he is a great boy. \\\")'),(15021,'dogtimemedia.com','guest2777','2008-10-28 12:54:13','(is usually when dogs over excited jumping etc.) from my experience, is after an absence'),(15022,'dogtimemedia.com','guest9568','2008-10-28 12:55:18','Exactly...   I dropped them both off with my mom who is retired & she cares for them while I am at work so they are never alone. But I have noticed that the excitement excels after long periods when I leave him .'),(15023,'dogtimemedia.com','guest8898','2008-10-28 14:01:58','hello pet people'),(15024,'dogtimemedia.com','guest8898','2008-10-28 14:02:57','i have three chihuahuas, what breeds do you all own?'),(15025,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-10-28 14:04:33','i own a pekingese beagle'),(15026,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-10-28 14:05:06','or a peagle as they\\\'re called'),(15027,'dogtimemedia.com','Valentine','2008-10-28 14:11:15','a peagle eh'),(15028,'dogtimemedia.com','Valentine','2008-10-28 14:11:25','i\\\'m personally a fan of Shih Pom'),(15029,'dogtimemedia.com','Valentine','2008-10-28 14:11:29','and Puggles'),(15030,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-10-28 14:17:54','i like peagles the best!'),(15031,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-10-28 14:18:23','they are mixing a lot of breeds nowadays and there are so very cute mixes out there'),(15032,'dogtimemedia.com','Valentine','2008-10-28 14:18:42','i agree, they call them \\\"designer\\\" dogs'),(15033,'dogtimemedia.com','Valentine','2008-10-28 14:19:01','as long as all the loveable dogs in shelters get adopted, people can call them whatever they want is what i think'),(15034,'dogtimemedia.com','guest8898','2008-10-28 14:41:55','i love puggs'),(15035,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=ViewsEditorialSectionPage&id=760f768a-8aa8-4da5-a5dc-6499cb4a28f9&&Headline=Orange+County','guest5488','2008-10-28 14:47:14','DOES THIS MUSLIM SWINE HAVE TO SAY ANYTHING ABOUT MUSLIM BAR