iately, and given supportive care before the venom causes symptoms like seizures. There is no home remedy for scorpion stings. \r\n\r\nIf your regular vet is closed now, bring her to an ER vet center in your area. You can see more about scorpion stings, here:'),(15964,'dogtimemedia.com','guest8071','2008-10-29 18:50:00','http://www.petplace.com/dogs/what-to-do-if-a-scorpion-stings-your-pet/page1.aspx'),(15965,'dogtimemedia.com','guest8071','2008-10-29 18:50:03','sorry about text'),(15966,'dogtimemedia.com','guest4659','2008-10-29 18:50:39','i caught the scorpion and it is small, it still has the stinger and my dof does not seem to have any pain, no swelling or redness'),(15967,'dogtimemedia.com','guest8071','2008-10-29 18:50:58','yea,but the sting'),(15968,'dogtimemedia.com','guest4659','2008-10-29 18:51:02','cool, thanks'),(15969,'dogtimemedia.com','guest8071','2008-10-29 18:51:08','can paralize your dog'),(15970,'dogtimemedia.com','guest8071','2008-10-29 18:51:35','u need to take ur dog to the vet if u really want to help him'),(15971,'dogtimemedia.com','guest5100','2008-10-29 18:52:56','hello'),(15972,'dogtimemedia.com','guest8071','2008-10-29 18:53:05','hey'),(15973,'dogtimemedia.com','guest8071','2008-10-29 18:53:08','whats up?'),(15974,'dogtimemedia.com','guest5100','2008-10-29 18:53:39','does anyone have any info on japanese spitz'),(15975,'dogtimemedia.com','guest5100','2008-10-29 18:54:12','such as how often should i have her groomed'),(15976,'dogtimemedia.com','guest8071','2008-10-29 18:54:35','hmm'),(15977,'dogtimemedia.com','PetProblemHelper','2008-10-29 18:54:48','ok'),(15978,'dogtimemedia.com','PetProblemHelper','2008-10-29 18:54:56','lemme check'),(15979,'dogtimemedia.com','guest5100','2008-10-29 18:55:08','thanks'),(15980,'dogtimemedia.com','PetProblemHelper','2008-10-29 18:55:28','np'),(15981,'dogtimemedia.com','PetProblemHelper','2008-10-29 18:56:04','how old is your japanese spitz?'),(15982,'dogtimemedia.com','guest5100','2008-10-29 18:56:29','she was born on july 4 2008'),(15983,'dogtimemedia.com','DogtimeMediaMVN1','2008-10-29 18:56:35','â€œWe highly encourage all guest users to sign up for a username. You can do so by clicking on â€œsignupâ€ right underneath this box. Once you register, PetChat community will be able to recognize you and weâ€™ll also send you email newsletters of upcoming hosted events. Hosted events will include things like live QA with renown trainers, vets, and professionals where you can come visit and ask questions, learn, and have fun.â€'),(15984,'dogtimemedia.com','PetProblemHelper','2008-10-29 18:56:37','ok'),(15985,'dogtimemedia.com','PetProblemHelper','2008-10-29 18:58:41','You need a small slicker brush and a small greyhound comb. Best way to brush is have puppy lay and his side and lightly brush the hair up from feet towards his head. Then brush a little hair toward the feet at a time...like you making a part to the skin do this all the way up the legs then do the body, neck,tail, between the legs and belly area are tender don\\\'t brush too hard. Brushing like this will ensure you don\\\'t miss any spots. Then comb the same way with the end of the comb that has teeth closer together. Good shampoos would be an oatmeal base...BioGroom, Espree, are good brands. Don\\\'t use Hartz, dish detergent or people shampoo all are to drying , to alkaline, and the pH levels are not for dog skin. You don\\\'t want to bathe more than once a month but if you have to because puppy got into mud, or a mess, make sure you use a good conditioner too.'),(15986,'dogtimemedia.com','PetProblemHelper','2008-10-29 18:58:46','this is how you groom it'),(15987,'dogtimemedia.com','PetProblemHelper','2008-10-29 18:58:55','i think'),(15988,'dogtimemedia.com','PetProblemHelper','2008-10-29 18:59:23','i would groom it 1 time every 2-4 days'),(15989,'dogtimemedia.com','PetProblemHelper','2008-10-29 18:59:32','by other peoples opinions'),(15990,'dogtimemedia.com','PetProblemHelper','2008-10-29 18:59:41','i hav