u guy\\\'s hear about the offer to obama?'),(24699,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 16:51:57','no'),(24700,'dogtimemedia.com','guest260','2008-11-11 16:52:00','im a dog trainer btw. what do you need help with?'),(24701,'dogtimemedia.com','guest260','2008-11-11 16:52:12','http://buzz.yahoo.com/buzzlog/92026/?fp=1'),(24702,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 16:52:55','well I have been thinking of getting a min pin puppy but hear they can have behavior problems and are hard to train, do you know anything about that?'),(24703,'dogtimemedia.com','guest260','2008-11-11 16:54:13','Pits are a little bit too independent and destructive as pups. But every dog has a different personality.'),(24704,'dogtimemedia.com','guest2159','2008-11-11 16:54:20','hey'),(24705,'dogtimemedia.com','guest260','2008-11-11 16:54:50','If you adopt from a very respectable breeder, you are most likely to get a dog bred for good behavior, not just looks'),(24706,'dogtimemedia.com','guest6703','2008-11-11 16:55:49','i luv dogs!!!!'),(24707,'dogtimemedia.com','guest260','2008-11-11 16:56:02','i have a pit client right now, and I say that if you have time and money for a trainer, go for it... but be aware that you might need to develop the dog\\\'s focus more then you need to with other dogs'),(24708,'dogtimemedia.com','guest2159','2008-11-11 16:56:14','hey i have seen a husky running around my neighborhood lately and i don\\\'t know what to do i\n called the pound and they have done nothiong to stop him'),(24709,'dogtimemedia.com','guest6703','2008-11-11 16:56:26','i have 200 dogs in my house'),(24710,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 16:56:38','call animal control'),(24711,'dogtimemedia.com','guest9359','2008-11-11 16:56:41','i have 2 chi puppies'),(24712,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 16:56:44','they can get him'),(24713,'dogtimemedia.com','guest6703','2008-11-11 16:56:47','ha ha'),(24714,'dogtimemedia.com','guest6703','2008-11-11 16:57:09','oh.. are serious???'),(24715,'dogtimemedia.com','guest6703','2008-11-11 16:57:20','I know'),(24716,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 16:57:33','Yeah, I was hoping to get a dog with good traits, but you never know, so I;m just trying to find out weather or not pins are easy to train or not...I will be a first time owner.'),(24717,'dogtimemedia.com','guest6703','2008-11-11 16:57:35','but I luv all of them!'),(24718,'dogtimemedia.com','guest6703','2008-11-11 16:58:20','dogs are soo cute'),(24719,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 16:59:27','so are there any min pin owners here?'),(24720,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 17:02:50','Does anyone have experience owning min pins or advice for a first time owner? I have never trained a dog before.'),(24721,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 17:04:24','any advice?'),(24722,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-11-11 17:04:27','training a dog takes time and patience.  the first week is going to be the hardest'),(24723,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-11-11 17:04:39','just getting the new dog used to his or her surroundings'),(24724,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 17:04:57','how much time would you have to dedicte in the first week on a daily basis?'),(24725,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-11-11 17:05:47','when i was raising my puppy, i worked close by and i would go home for lunch, take him out and spend my lunch hour with him'),(24726,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-11-11 17:06:05','i would say spend a couple hours each night with the new pup playing, taking him out for walks'),(24727,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-11-11 17:07:48','be consistent with the commands you use with your dog'),(24728,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 17:07:58','so just a few hours of training a day will help my puppy learn what he should know?'),(24729,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 17:09:06','I would think that consistency would be a big part of the process, defnintely.'),(24730,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-11-11 17:09:06','i wouldn\\\'t necessarily say that - but spending time with your new pup is very important to get him used to you and his new surroundings'),(24731,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-11-11 17:09:28','use treats to reward him when you\\\'re training'),(24732,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-11-11 17:10:53','dogs don\\\'t respond if you yell at them or hit them - if he does have an accident in the house and you are there to see it, you need to discipline right away'),(24733,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 17:11:19','I know I\\\'m going to want to spend a bunch of time with him, but I don\\\'t want to burn him out with constant training, I have heard that its good to train with breaks in between for puppies.'),(24734,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-11-11 17:11:24','if he has an accident when you are out of the house, punishing him won\\\'t do much good because he won\\\'t necessarily know what he is being punished for'),(24735,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-11-11 17:11:40','of course - you want to make training fun for both people!'),(24736,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 17:12:16','wow I am so excited. I cant wait to start.'),(24737,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 17:12:50','the one thing I have heard about min pins is tht they bark alot and can be harder to train than other breeds. is this true?'),(24738,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-11-11 17:13:05','my dog is a little over 4 years old and when i think back about training him, i do smile because it was fun'),(24739,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-11-11 17:13:34','i don\\\'t know much about min pin'),(24740,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 17:14:20','I\\\'m really excited because I cant wait to have a constant companion.'),(24741,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 17:14:52','being with friends and loved ones is great, but having a happy dog to come home to sounds so wonderful.'),(24742,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 17:15:14','I just hope this is the right time in my life for a dog.'),(24743,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-11-11 17:15:14','i have to say from personal experience that it\\\'s great to come home to a dog'),(24744,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-11-11 17:15:51','well just make sure you have the time for the new pup and that you can provide a loving home for him'),(24745,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 17:17:59','yeah, I will be living in an apartment and I;m  student. My landlord LOVES pets, so no problem there, and I cant wait to train a puppy and make him/her a part of my life, but I just want to make sure it\\\'s ok to have a dog while being a student. I have plenty of time, but some argue against it.'),(24746,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-11-11 17:19:43','i would just make sure you have the time - that is the key'),(24747,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-11-11 17:20:03','dogs need exercise, love and attention'),(24748,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 17:21:57','Yes. I will be gone for a few hours daily, and home the rest of the time with the dog. I plan to take it with me to see friends to socialize it.'),(24749,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 17:23:17','I want to be SURE that is enough time. I feel ready, but I hate seeing dogs in shelters and I wont let my dog be one of them! so I want to get alot of info before getting a dog for sure.'),(24750,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 17:24:31','you are the first live person I have spoken with about it, other than that its been lots and lots of research!'),(24751,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-11-11 17:29:40','no problem - i grew up with dogs as a kid so i kinda knew what to expect when i got my own dog'),(24752,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-11-11 17:30:37','if you are thinking of adopting a dog from a shelter, there is an interview process and they do ask you questions and let you spend some time with the dog, you also fill out a questionaire about if you\\\'re ready for a dog'),(24753,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 17:32:22','yeah, I had a dog living with my parents but we had to put him down, by the age of three he had such bad hips he couldn\\\'t walk and was no longer happy. He was in pain, i feel we did the right thing, but I miss the companionship and fel like I never really got the full experience because he died so young. I just want to do my homework before embarking on this on my own.'),(24754,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 17:33:10','wow that sounds really great, that way I really cant go wrong. thats a good idea, making sure the dogs get really good homes.'),(24755,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-11-11 17:34:38','yeah they don\\\'t want to see dogs come back to the shelter and they want the dog to go into a loving and good home'),(24756,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 17:36:38','do you think i could find one of those question sheets\n online?'),(24757,'www.hindustantimes.com/StoryPage/StoryPage.aspx?sectionName=HomePage&id=730350b5-c267-4f41-bb9d-657977ed67e7&&Headline=New+rage+against+the+machine','guest492','2008-11-11 17:37:21','Sagarika, You ...... Dont you understand what is making Hindus angry. 1000s being killed everyday and noone is doing anything about it.. Get a life and shame on reporters like you calling indus as terrorists and making a fool of us all....'),(24758,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-11-11 17:38:26','i\\\'ve seen an are you ready for a dog quiz on several websites - try petflog.com'),(24759,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 17:38:53','thanks i will'),(24760,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 17:43:06','Wow, thank you for the helpful quiz, I passed it!'),(24761,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-11-11 17:43:39','that\\\'s good!'),(24762,'dogtimemedia.com','guest3874','2008-11-11 17:44:00','I really appreciate the help and tips, Thanks so much for taking the time to help :)'),(24763,'dogtimemedia.com','coop14','2008-11-11 17:44:2